40	\section{Introduction}
41	\label{sec:intro}
42	% ============================================================
43	
44	Test-time scaling (TTS)---generating multiple candidate outputs and selecting the best one---has emerged as a powerful strategy for improving LLM performance \citep{wang2023selfconsistency,snell2024scaling,brown2024large}.
45	Self-consistency \citep{wang2023selfconsistency} and minimum Bayes risk (MBR) decoding \citep{eikema2022sampling} demonstrate that multi-sample strategies can substantially outperform single-sample greedy decoding on reasoning and translation tasks.
46	
47	Structured information extraction (IE)---extracting typed entity sets and relational triples from text---presents a fundamentally different challenge.
48	Unlike multiple-choice reasoning where answers are discrete tokens, IE outputs are \emph{sets of structured objects} with partial credit: two candidate entity sets may share some entities but differ on others.
49	This structural richness suggests that consistency-based confidence signals could be particularly informative, as they can measure agreement at multiple granularities (exact match, entity overlap, structural similarity).
